msgid "Our attempt to associate the probability of a measurement with the inner product squared means we need the magnitude of each vector to be 1. That is, $|\\langle v|v\\rangle|^2 = 1$ for all $|v\\rangle$, since the probability of a thing in state $|v\\rangle$ being in state $|v\\rangle$ is 100%. This is known as the \"normalization condition\".\n"
msgstr ""

